## 7. Schedule

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Schedule type | Fixed |
| Repeat | Daily |
| Times | 12:00 PM and 12:00 AM (twice a day) |
| Start | 10/28/2026 |
| End | 08/28/2027 |
| Time zone | (UTC+02:00) Cairo |
| Parameters | None |

- Add an email address under **Failure notifications** (Schedule tab of the pipeline).
- The 12-hour gap means runs will not overlap. (To our knowledge Fabric has no setting that prevents overlapping runs.)

---

## 8. Permissions

- The schedule runs under the identity of whoever created or last edited it. That identity needs:
  - **Contributor** on the workspace.
  - **Read** access to the KQL database `eh_fleet` (Bronze and Alerts use its token).
- Different owners on the notebooks do not matter as long as this identity has Contributor.

---

## 9. Known Notes and Limitations

1. **The Eventstreams must stay Running** at all times, because the pipeline only reads what has already been collected in KQL.
2. **`vehicle_key` in `gold.fact_alerts`:** `alerts_load` runs before `batch_job_2`, so on the first run `vehicle_key` is NULL. On later runs it is filled from the previous run's `dim_vehicle`. Alternative: move `alerts_load` after `batch_job_2` (there is no reverse dependency).
3. **`lateness_sec`** is tied to the `run_manifest.json` of a single run. If Bronze holds data from other runs the values are inaccurate, and the notebook prints MISMATCH without stopping.
4. **Spark capacity:** open interactive sessions consume the same capacity. Close sessions you do not need before scheduled runs. The two 120 s Wait activities are a workaround for this; if failures come back, increase the Wait time or Retry count.
5. **`alerts_load`** reads the whole `alert_events` table every time (no watermark). Acceptable at the current volume.
6. **Gate 1:** on FAIL, Silver has already been written, and the pipeline stops before `alerts_load` and `batch_job_2`.

---

## 10. Quick Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| An activity fails after about 20s and succeeds on retry | Spark capacity | Increase the Wait activities (for example to 180 s), increase Retry, use Increasing Delay, and close open sessions |
| `batch_job_1` fails in the manifest cell | `run_manifest.json` or `run_summary.json` is missing | Check `Files/evidence` in `lh_fleet` |
| `batch_job_2` fails with "table already exists" | `IF NOT EXISTS` missing in Cell 3 | Add it |
| The If Condition fails or the Fail activity runs | Gate 1 returned FAIL | Open the `batch_job_1` output and read the exitValue |
| The If Condition expression errors | The `output.result.exitValue` path or the activity name is wrong | Check the Output in Monitor and confirm the name is `batch_job_1` |
| Bronze is slow or exceeds its timeout | 12 hours of data per run | Increase the timeout |

---

## 11. Follow-up Checklist

- [ ] Confirm the first scheduled run started on time.
- [ ] Review the duration of Bronze and `batch_job_1` and adjust the timeouts if needed.
- [ ] Add the Failure notifications email.
- [ ] Replace `session.stop()` with `notebook.exit` in the remaining notebooks.
- [ ] Check the Spark capacity message in the Output of the failed attempts (from the first run, before the Waits were added).
- [ ] Watch the first few scheduled runs to confirm the 120 s Waits are enough, since one clean run is not proof.
- [ ] Make a final decision on the order of `alerts_load` and `batch_job_2` (the `vehicle_key` issue).{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Imports and configuration\n","Sets the session time zone to UTC (matches Kusto and Bronze), the job name, and two timestamp formats. The watermark text keeps microseconds so no row is reloaded."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"a5288049-6b3b-4c17-ba41-e1bba1e2d39e"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import json\n","import uuid\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","\n","import fleet_shared as fs\n","from pyspark.sql import functions as F, Window\n","from pyspark.sql.types import (StructType, StructField, StringType,\n","                               BooleanType, ArrayType)\n","\n","spark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.session.timeZone\", \"UTC\")   # match Kusto / Bronze timestamps\n","\n","JOB_NAME = \"nb_p2_batch_job_1\"\n","TS_FMT = \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%f\"          # used inside SQL TIMESTAMP literals\n","WM_FMT = \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%fZ\"         # watermark text keeps microseconds (no reloaded rows)"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":5,"statement_ids":[5],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:32.6913903Z","session_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:32.6925489Z","execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:04.5934657Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:05.1579324Z","parent_msg_id":"144db010-74c5-441c-97b6-23bddcb58966"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 5, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"bba051d3-cf1c-4125-bfdf-2176789b2da9"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Run manifest and job settings\n","Loads `Files/evidence/run_manifest.json` (`wall_start`, `sim_start`, acceleration factor A) for `lateness_sec`, and compares `run_summary.json` with the Bronze row counts so a manifest from a different run is noticed. Also holds the thresholds for the sequence flags, the vehicle-activity check and Gate 1.\n","\n","**Notes:** the manifest describes one run. If Bronze contains several runs, `lateness_sec` is only right for the run in the manifest. The thresholds should be compared with the printed `fs.DEFAULT_RULES` of the library."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"c63258e8-2b47-4f3f-88bb-00f6831d4cae"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# ---- Run manifest (needed for lateness_sec) and job settings ----\n","MANIFEST_PATH = \"Files/evidence/run_manifest.json\"     # must be the manifest of the run that is in Bronze\n","SUMMARY_PATH  = \"Files/evidence/run_summary.json\"\n","\n","def _iso_to_epoch(s):\n","    return datetime.fromisoformat(s.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\")).timestamp()\n","\n","def load_manifest():\n","    m = spark.read.option(\"multiLine\", \"true\").json(MANIFEST_PATH).first()\n","    return {\"run_id\": m[\"run_id\"],\n","            \"sim_start\": _iso_to_epoch(m[\"sim_start\"]),\n","            \"wall_start\": _iso_to_epoch(m[\"wall_start\"]),\n","            \"A\": float(m[\"acceleration_factor\"]),\n","            \"fast_mode\": bool(m[\"fast_mode\"])}\n","\n","def check_manifest_against_bronze():\n","    \"\"\"Print whether the manifest/summary belong to the data in Bronze. Prints only, never stops the job.\"\"\"\n","    s = spark.read.option(\"multiLine\", \"true\").json(SUMMARY_PATH).first()\n","    per = s[\"per_signal\"].asDict()\n","    ok = True\n","    for sig in [\"gps\", \"engine\", \"fuel\", \"temperature\"]:\n","        n = spark.table(f\"bronze.bronze_{sig}_raw\").count()\n","        same = (n == per[sig])\n","        ok = ok and same\n","        print(f\"{sig:12s} summary={per[sig]:>7} bronze={n:>7} {'OK' if same else 'MISMATCH'}\")\n","    print(\"run_id:\", s[\"run_id\"], \"| messages_sent:\", s[\"messages_sent\"])\n","    if not ok:\n","        print(\"WARNING: the manifest does not match Bronze, lateness_sec would be wrong. Get the right files first.\")\n","    if MANIFEST[\"fast_mode\"]:\n","        print(\"WARNING: fast_mode = true, lateness_sec is meaningless for this run.\")\n","\n","MANIFEST = load_manifest()\n","print(MANIFEST)\n","check_manifest_against_bronze()\n","\n","# ---- Settings for the sequence flags, vehicle check and Gate 1 ----\n","ENABLE_ACTIVE_CHECK = True      # reject rows whose vehicle is not active on the event date\n","SPIKE_DELTA_C       = 8.0       # temperature: jump from the previous reading above this -> SPIKE\n","FLATLINE_N          = 10        # temperature: this many identical readings in a row -> FLATLINE\n","MAX_JUMP_SPEED_KMH  = 200.0     # gps: implied speed between two consecutive points above this -> IMPOSSIBLE_JUMP\n","GATE_MAX_INVALID_PCT = 5.0      # quality_gate_max_invalid_pct\n","\n","# Compare these thresholds with the library rules and edit the numbers above if they differ\n","print(fs.DEFAULT_RULES)"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":6,"statement_ids":[6],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:32.906716Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:05.1602109Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.470453Z","parent_msg_id":"66d539e5-5ad3-48b7-b029-91820a482b30"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 6, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["{'run_id': 'run-20261026-043040-smoke', 'sim_start': 1767248520.0, 'wall_start': 1792989040.0, 'A': 50.0, 'fast_mode': False}\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["gps          summary=  30895 bronze=  30895 OK\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["engine       summary=  30926 bronze=  30926 OK\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["fuel         summary=   5176 bronze=   5176 OK\ntemperature  summary=   7197 bronze=   7197 OK\nrun_id: run-20261026-043040-smoke | messages_sent: 74194\n{'idle_speed_threshold_kmh': 2.0, 'idle_minutes_threshold': 5.0, 'speeding_tolerance_kmh': 5.0, 'gps_accuracy_max_meters': 50.0, 'deviation_consecutive_readings': 3.0, 'gps_jump_max_kmh': 200.0, 'speed_max_kmh': 130.0, 'engine_rpm_max': 4000.0, 'engine_temperature_max_c': 130.0, 'cargo_temperature_valid_min_c': -40.0, 'cargo_temperature_valid_max_c': 60.0, 'temperature_spike_c': 8.0, 'flatline_readings': 20.0, 'future_timestamp_tolerance_minutes': 5.0, 'expected_interval_gps_sec': 10.0, 'expected_interval_engine_sec': 10.0, 'expected_interval_fuel_sec': 60.0, 'expected_interval_temp_sec': 30.0, 'offline_missed_intervals': 3.0, 'late_data_watermark_minutes': 10.0, 'sequence_gap_grace_minutes': 120.0, 'dq_window_minutes': 10.0, 'invalid_rate_alert_pct': 2.0, 'quality_gate_max_invalid_pct': 5.0, 'score_weight_speeding': 35.0, 'score_weight_idling': 30.0, 'score_weight_deviation': 20.0, 'score_weight_lateness': 15.0, 'score_limit_speeding_pct': 5.0, 'score_limit_idling_pct': 10.0, 'score_limit_deviation_episodes': 2.0, 'score_limit_late_minutes': 60.0}\n"]}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"602ebb56-da00-4d5e-85cd-7436e3b874dc"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Window selection\n","Lower bound is the saved watermark in `ops.ops_watermark`; upper bound is the newest Bronze `ingestion_time`. Only rows in (lower, upper] are processed."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"c85ab6c8-de47-4cc4-a2cb-40c18b95a359"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def get_window(signal):\n","    \"\"\"Return (lower, upper): lower = saved watermark, upper = newest Bronze ingestion_time.\"\"\"\n","    lower = spark.sql(\n","        f\"SELECT to_timestamp(watermark_utc) AS w FROM ops.ops_watermark WHERE signal='{signal}'\"\n","    ).first()[\"w\"]\n","    upper = (spark.table(f\"bronze.bronze_{signal}_raw\")\n","                  .agg(F.max(\"ingestion_time\")).first()[0])\n","    return lower, upper"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":7,"statement_ids":[7],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:33.2980249Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.4729062Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.6712714Z","parent_msg_id":"6d0ddf9d-22ef-4897-a536-811fbe4ff094"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 7, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"3ba64324-7b34-4f22-8513-cdd29f2da286"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Lookups and validation\n","`load_lookups` builds the known vehicles, known trips and tank capacity (latest row per vehicle by `updated_at`). `validate` runs `fleet_shared.validate_message` per row through a UDF and splits good and bad rows.\n","\n","**Vehicle active check:** a valid row is also rejected when its vehicle has no `ref_vehicles_raw` version that is active on the event date (`active_from <= date <= active_to`, empty means open ended). Such rows go to the DLQ as `UNKNOWN_VEHICLE` with the message \"Vehicle not active at event time\". Switch it off with `ENABLE_ACTIVE_CHECK = False`.\n","\n","**Pending:** the simulated `now` argument for the future-timestamp check."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"e85d77bb-51e7-4086-b82f-2182ceeaf050"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["RES_SCHEMA = StructType([\n","    StructField(\"ok\", BooleanType()),\n","    StructField(\"error_code\", StringType()),\n","    StructField(\"error_message\", StringType()),\n","    StructField(\"retryable\", BooleanType()),\n","    StructField(\"flags\", ArrayType(StringType())),\n","    StructField(\"record_json\", StringType()),\n","])\n","\n","\n","def load_lookups():\n","    \"\"\"Reference sets passed to fleet_shared so it can detect UNKNOWN_* and tank overflow.\"\"\"\n","    veh = spark.table(\"ref.ref_vehicles_raw\")\n","    known_vehicles = {r[0] for r in veh.select(\"vehicle_id\").distinct().collect()}\n","    known_trips = {r[0] for r in spark.table(\"ref.ref_trips\").select(\"trip_id\").distinct().collect()}\n","\n","    # One capacity per vehicle: take the latest row by updated_at (all columns are strings)\n","    w = Window.partitionBy(\"vehicle_id\").orderBy(F.col(\"updated_at\").desc())\n","    latest = (veh.withColumn(\"rn\", F.row_number().over(w)).where(\"rn = 1\")\n","                 .select(\"vehicle_id\", F.col(\"fuel_tank_capacity_liters\").cast(\"double\").alias(\"cap\")))\n","    tank_cap = {r[\"vehicle_id\"]: r[\"cap\"] for r in latest.collect() if r[\"cap\"] is not None}\n","    return known_vehicles, known_trips, tank_cap\n","\n","\n","def make_validate_udf(known_vehicles, known_trips, tank_cap, now=None):\n","    \"\"\"Build the UDF with the lookups captured in its closure (small sets, shipped to executors).\n","    `now` is the SIMULATED time (naive datetime) used by the library for the future-timestamp check.\"\"\"\n","    @F.udf(RES_SCHEMA)\n","    def validate_udf(raw):\n","        r = fs.validate_message(raw, known_vehicles=known_vehicles,\n","                                known_trips=known_trips,\n","                                tank_capacity_by_vehicle=tank_cap,\n","                                now=now)\n","        return (r.ok, r.error_code, r.error_message, r.retryable,\n","                list(r.flags or []), json.dumps(r.record) if r.record else None)\n","    return validate_udf\n","\n","\n","def simulated_now(upper):\n","    \"\"\"Simulated time at the newest Bronze ingestion_time: sim_start + (wall elapsed) * A.\n","    Returned as a naive datetime, because fleet_shared compares it with naive datetimes.\"\"\"\n","    up_epoch = upper.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp()\n","    sim_epoch = MANIFEST[\"sim_start\"] + (up_epoch - MANIFEST[\"wall_start\"]) * MANIFEST[\"A\"]\n","    return datetime.fromtimestamp(sim_epoch, tz=timezone.utc).replace(tzinfo=None)\n","\n","\n","def load_vehicle_intervals():\n","    \"\"\"One row per vehicle version: the dates in which that version was active (NULL = open ended).\"\"\"\n","    return (spark.table(\"ref.ref_vehicles_raw\")\n","                 .select(F.col(\"vehicle_id\").alias(\"iv_vehicle\"),\n","                         F.to_date(F.trim(\"active_from\")).alias(\"iv_from\"),\n","                         F.to_date(F.trim(\"active_to\")).alias(\"iv_to\")))\n","\n","\n","def split_by_vehicle_activity(good):\n","    \"\"\"Split validated rows into (active, inactive). Inactive rows are returned in the DLQ shape\n","    (error_code UNKNOWN_VEHICLE, message says the vehicle was not active at event time).\"\"\"\n","    g = (good\n","         .withColumn(\"_veh\", F.get_json_object(\"v.record_json\", \"$.vehicle_id\"))\n","         .withColumn(\"_ev_date\", F.to_date(F.get_json_object(\"v.record_json\", \"$.event_time\").cast(\"timestamp\"))))\n","    iv = F.broadcast(load_vehicle_intervals())\n","    cond = ((F.col(\"_veh\") == F.col(\"iv_vehicle\")) &\n","            (F.col(\"iv_from\").isNull() | (F.col(\"iv_from\") <= F.col(\"_ev_date\"))) &\n","            (F.col(\"iv_to\").isNull() | (F.col(\"_ev_date\") <= F.col(\"iv_to\"))))\n","    active = g.join(iv, cond, \"left_semi\").drop(\"_veh\", \"_ev_date\")\n","    inactive = (g.join(iv, cond, \"left_anti\").drop(\"_veh\", \"_ev_date\")\n","                 .withColumn(\"v\", F.struct(\n","                     F.lit(False).alias(\"ok\"),\n","                     F.lit(\"UNKNOWN_VEHICLE\").alias(\"error_code\"),\n","                     F.lit(\"Vehicle not active at event time\").alias(\"error_message\"),\n","                     F.lit(True).alias(\"retryable\"),\n","                     F.col(\"v.flags\").alias(\"flags\"),\n","                     F.col(\"v.record_json\").alias(\"record_json\"))))\n","    return active, inactive\n","\n","\n","def validate(signal, lower, upper, lookups):\n","    \"\"\"Read the window from Bronze, validate every row, split into good and bad.\"\"\"\n","    udf = make_validate_udf(*lookups, now=simulated_now(upper))\n","    df = (spark.table(f\"bronze.bronze_{signal}_raw\")\n","               .where((F.col(\"ingestion_time\") > F.lit(lower)) &\n","                      (F.col(\"ingestion_time\") <= F.lit(upper))))\n","    validated = df.withColumn(\"v\", udf(\"raw_value\")).cache()\n","    n_bronze = validated.count()\n","    good = validated.where(\"v.ok = true\")\n","    bad = validated.where(\"v.ok = false\")\n","\n","    # Extra check: the vehicle must be active on the event date (ref_vehicles_raw active_from / active_to)\n","    if ENABLE_ACTIVE_CHECK:\n","        good, inactive = split_by_vehicle_activity(good)\n","        bad = bad.unionByName(inactive)\n","    return validated, good, bad, n_bronze"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":8,"statement_ids":[8],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:33.52224Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.6736868Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.856849Z","parent_msg_id":"e8706221-9e1d-4357-838c-ef3263acf210"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 8, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"56d1105f-aea7-44ff-a72d-77fc6c81cd66"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Dead-letter queue\n","Writes rejected rows with error code, raw text and Bronze arrival time. Idempotent: deletes the DLQ rows of the same signal and window first, so a re-run never doubles them."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"aad074f0-cdff-44a0-b9c4-f9ee74dc11be"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def write_dlq(bad, signal, batch_id, lower, upper):\n","    \"\"\"Write rejected rows to ops.dlq_events. Idempotent: clears the same window first.\"\"\"\n","    spark.sql(f\"\"\"DELETE FROM ops.dlq_events\n","                  WHERE signal='{signal}' AND stage='BATCH'\n","                    AND bronze_ingestion_time > TIMESTAMP'{lower:{TS_FMT}}'\n","                    AND bronze_ingestion_time <= TIMESTAMP'{upper:{TS_FMT}}'\"\"\")\n","\n","    dlq = bad.select(\n","        F.expr(\"uuid()\").alias(\"dlq_id\"),\n","        F.lit(batch_id).alias(\"batch_id\"),\n","        F.lit(\"BATCH\").alias(\"stage\"),\n","        F.lit(signal).alias(\"signal\"),\n","        F.col(\"v.error_code\").alias(\"error_code\"),\n","        F.col(\"v.error_message\").alias(\"error_message\"),\n","        # get_json_object does not fail on broken JSON (returns NULL instead)\n","        F.get_json_object(\"raw_value\", \"$.event_id\").alias(\"event_id\"),\n","        \"raw_value\", \"source_type\", \"source_file\", \"file_line\",\n","        F.col(\"ingestion_time\").alias(\"bronze_ingestion_time\"),\n","        F.col(\"v.retryable\").alias(\"is_retryable\"),\n","        F.current_timestamp().alias(\"created_at\"),\n","    )\n","    n_dlq = dlq.count()\n","    dlq.write.mode(\"append\").saveAsTable(\"ops.dlq_events\")\n","    return n_dlq"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":9,"statement_ids":[9],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:33.7769325Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:19.8591268Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.0282611Z","parent_msg_id":"6062ed47-0a03-4d90-811f-7b7aa45fb983"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 9, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"43663210-f04d-41f3-a396-b9a3ac5daa0c"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Parse and enrich\n","Turns the validated JSON into typed columns, stores `dq_flags` as comma-separated text (NULL when no flags), and adds route, driver and cargo from a broadcast join with `ref_trips`.\n","\n","**`lateness_sec`:** `expected_arrival = wall_start + (event_time - sim_start) / A`, then `lateness_sec = ingestion_time - expected_arrival`, in seconds. `event_time` is simulated time and `ingestion_time` is wall-clock time, so the simulated time is converted first. `ingestion_time` is the KQL ingestion time, so the value is approximate."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"13e2ad6e-17d9-4845-b793-187bf573c7a5"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def parse_and_enrich(good, signal):\n","    \"\"\"Turn the cleaned JSON into real columns and add route/driver/cargo from ref_trips.\"\"\"\n","    # Column list comes from the library, so it works for every signal\n","    common = (\"schema_version INT, event_id STRING, vehicle_id STRING, trip_id STRING, \"\n","              \"device_id STRING, event_time STRING, sequence_number BIGINT\")\n","    sig_cols = \", \".join(f\"{n} {t}\" for n, t in fs.SIGNAL_FIELDS[signal])\n","    rec_ddl = f\"{common}, {sig_cols}\"\n","\n","    parsed = (good\n","        .withColumn(\"r\", F.from_json(\"v.record_json\", rec_ddl))\n","        .select(\"r.*\",\n","        F.when(F.size(\"v.flags\") > 0, F.concat_ws(\",\", \"v.flags\")).alias(\"dq_flags\"),\n","        \"ingestion_time\")\n","        .withColumn(\"event_time\", F.to_timestamp(\"event_time\"))\n","        .withColumn(\"event_date\", F.to_date(\"event_time\")))        # partition column\n","\n","    # ref_trips is small, so broadcast it\n","    trips = spark.table(\"ref.ref_trips\").select(\"trip_id\", \"route_id\", \"driver_id\", \"cargo_type_id\")\n","    enriched = parsed.join(F.broadcast(trips), \"trip_id\", \"left\")\n","\n","    # lateness_sec = ingestion_time - expected_arrival (both as epoch seconds), where\n","    # expected_arrival = wall_start + (event_time - sim_start) / A   (values from run_manifest.json)\n","    expected_arrival = (F.lit(MANIFEST[\"wall_start\"]) +\n","                        (F.col(\"event_time\").cast(\"double\") - F.lit(MANIFEST[\"sim_start\"])) / F.lit(MANIFEST[\"A\"]))\n","    return enriched.withColumn(\"lateness_sec\",\n","                               F.round(F.col(\"ingestion_time\").cast(\"double\") - expected_arrival, 3))"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":10,"statement_ids":[10],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:33.9191731Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.0304353Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.2212862Z","parent_msg_id":"40143adf-263f-48fa-8c41-7ca5c2506457"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 10, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"4dd6929d-d6df-4174-a05c-515561e0276f"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Deduplication\n","Keeps the first copy per `event_id`. Near-duplicates (same vehicle, signal and event time with a new `event_id`) are not removed yet. To be replaced by the library rule."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"c5c36dd0-4211-483a-9d11-32a90919fa00"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def dedup_batch(enriched):\n","    \"\"\"Keep one row per event_id (fs.DEDUP_KEY). TEMPORARY rule: first copy that arrived.\"\"\"\n","    w = Window.partitionBy(\"event_id\").orderBy(F.col(\"ingestion_time\").asc())\n","    deduped = (enriched.withColumn(\"rn\", F.row_number().over(w))\n","                       .where(\"rn = 1\").drop(\"rn\"))\n","    n_ok = enriched.count()\n","    n_kept = deduped.count()\n","    return deduped, n_kept, n_ok - n_kept     # (dataframe, rows kept, duplicates removed)"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":11,"statement_ids":[11],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:34.1814867Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.2236318Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.4064072Z","parent_msg_id":"24070b9e-a871-4ced-a097-260ef1e93b31"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 11, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"11cf2dec-2ed3-4ee1-a2e5-31b073c53f14"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Sequence flags (SPIKE, FLATLINE, IMPOSSIBLE_JUMP)\n","These flags need the previous row of the same vehicle, so they are computed on the deduplicated batch with window functions and appended to `dq_flags`.\n","\n","- **temperature:** `SPIKE` when the value differs from the previous reading of the same vehicle and sensor by more than `SPIKE_DELTA_C`; `FLATLINE` when the last `FLATLINE_N` readings are identical.\n","- **gps:** `IMPOSSIBLE_JUMP` when the distance to the previous point divided by the time gap exceeds `MAX_JUMP_SPEED_KMH` (haversine distance).\n","- **engine, fuel:** no sequence flags.\n","\n","**Limits:** the previous row is looked up inside the current batch only, so the first row of each vehicle in a batch is never flagged. The point after a jump is compared with the jump point, so it can be flagged too."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"62934902-13b6-4ebd-8b86-4bbdd77320d8"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def _append_flag(col, cond, flag):\n","    \"\"\"Add a flag to the comma separated dq_flags text (NULL stays NULL when the condition is false).\"\"\"\n","    return F.when(cond, F.concat_ws(\",\", F.col(col), F.lit(flag))).otherwise(F.col(col))\n","\n","\n","def add_sequence_flags(df, signal):\n","    \"\"\"Flags that need the previous row of the same vehicle (computed inside the batch only).\n","    NULL dq_flags still means \"no flag raised\", and a batch's first row per vehicle has no previous row.\"\"\"\n","    if signal == \"temperature\":\n","        w = Window.partitionBy(\"vehicle_id\", \"sensor_id\").orderBy(\"event_time\", \"sequence_number\")\n","        w_n = w.rowsBetween(-(FLATLINE_N - 1), 0)\n","        t = F.col(\"temperature_value\")\n","        spike = F.abs(t - F.lag(\"temperature_value\").over(w)) > F.lit(SPIKE_DELTA_C)\n","        flat = ((F.count(t).over(w_n) == F.lit(FLATLINE_N)) &\n","                (F.min(t).over(w_n) == F.max(t).over(w_n)))\n","        return (df.withColumn(\"_spike\", spike).withColumn(\"_flat\", flat)\n","                  .withColumn(\"dq_flags\", _append_flag(\"dq_flags\", F.col(\"_spike\"), \"SPIKE\"))\n","                  .withColumn(\"dq_flags\", _append_flag(\"dq_flags\", F.col(\"_flat\"), \"FLATLINE\"))\n","                  .drop(\"_spike\", \"_flat\"))\n","\n","    if signal == \"gps\":\n","        w = Window.partitionBy(\"vehicle_id\").orderBy(\"event_time\", \"sequence_number\")\n","        lat1, lon1 = F.radians(F.lag(\"latitude\").over(w)), F.radians(F.lag(\"longitude\").over(w))\n","        lat2, lon2 = F.radians(F.col(\"latitude\")), F.radians(F.col(\"longitude\"))\n","        a = (F.pow(F.sin((lat2 - lat1) / 2), 2) +\n","             F.cos(lat1) * F.cos(lat2) * F.pow(F.sin((lon2 - lon1) / 2), 2))\n","        dist_km = 2 * 6371.0 * F.asin(F.sqrt(a))\n","        dt_h = (F.col(\"event_time\").cast(\"double\") -\n","                F.lag(\"event_time\").over(w).cast(\"double\")) / 3600.0\n","        jump = (dt_h > 0) & ((dist_km / dt_h) > F.lit(MAX_JUMP_SPEED_KMH))\n","        return (df.withColumn(\"_jump\", jump)\n","                  .withColumn(\"dq_flags\", _append_flag(\"dq_flags\", F.col(\"_jump\"), \"IMPOSSIBLE_JUMP\"))\n","                  .drop(\"_jump\"))\n","\n","    return df      # engine and fuel have no sequence flags"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":12,"statement_ids":[12],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:34.3604407Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.4086113Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.5772217Z","parent_msg_id":"e5f483e7-0dde-4342-aa73-16488d09104d"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 12, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"606fe44a-f56d-4faf-bd22-8acf3ca5b6de"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## MERGE into Silver\n","Inserts only `event_id`s not yet in Silver, so a re-run adds nothing."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"8f94009f-95f6-4018-b957-90f2e0211afc"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def merge_silver(deduped, signal):\n","    \"\"\"Insert only event_ids that are not in Silver yet. Re-runs add nothing.\"\"\"\n","    silver_cols = spark.table(f\"silver.silver_{signal}\").columns   # column order from the table\n","    deduped.select(*silver_cols).createOrReplaceTempView(\"batch_silver\")\n","    spark.sql(f\"\"\"MERGE INTO silver.silver_{signal} t\n","                  USING batch_silver s ON t.event_id = s.event_id\n","                  WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *\"\"\")"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":13,"statement_ids":[13],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:34.610208Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.5793717Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.7555303Z","parent_msg_id":"4ffa559f-193b-40ee-8508-bb91414ddd9d"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 13, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"874977b0-4acf-4b02-ad3d-bef62b02f0b1"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Logging and watermark\n","One row per signal per run in `ops.ops_ingestion_log` (Bronze, Silver, DLQ and duplicate counts, status). The watermark moves only after a successful run."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"b39c7474-e32a-4f6e-97b7-5a8d0d646acf"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def write_log(batch_id, signal, lower, upper, n_bronze, n_silver, n_dlq, n_dups,\n","              status, started, error=None):\n","    \"\"\"One row in ops.ops_ingestion_log per signal per run.\"\"\"\n","    row = [(str(uuid.uuid4()), batch_id, JOB_NAME, signal, \"BATCH\", None,\n","            f\"{lower:{WM_FMT}}\", f\"{upper:{WM_FMT}}\",\n","            n_bronze, n_silver, n_dlq, n_dups, status,\n","            (error or \"\")[:1000] or None, started, datetime.utcnow())]\n","    ddl = (\"log_id string, batch_id string, job_name string, signal string, stage string, \"\n","           \"source_file string, window_start_utc string, window_end_utc string, \"\n","           \"rows_bronze long, rows_silver long, rows_dlq long, rows_duplicates_removed long, \"\n","           \"status string, error_message string, started_at timestamp, finished_at timestamp\")\n","    spark.createDataFrame(row, ddl).write.mode(\"append\").saveAsTable(\"ops.ops_ingestion_log\")\n","\n","\n","def set_watermark(signal, upper):\n","    \"\"\"Save the new watermark. Must be the LAST step of a successful run.\"\"\"\n","    spark.sql(f\"\"\"UPDATE ops.ops_watermark\n","                  SET watermark_utc = '{upper:{WM_FMT}}', updated_at = current_timestamp()\n","                  WHERE signal = '{signal}'\"\"\")"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":14,"statement_ids":[14],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:34.8923005Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:20.7576211Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:21.9747047Z","parent_msg_id":"98a1a8e6-1e60-459e-81b6-c3c8556d5935"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 14, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"ed3b6f87-8429-4967-af75-0b8337420cfa"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Orchestration for one signal\n","Window, validate, DLQ, enrich, dedup, sequence flags, MERGE, log, watermark. On failure it logs FAILED and leaves the watermark unchanged so the run can be repeated. Check: bronze = silver + dlq + duplicates."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"c3a17a7c-1b5a-47c2-b730-12bd8e83b9c3"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def process_signal(signal):\n","    \"\"\"Full batch job 1 for one signal: validate -> DLQ / Silver -> log -> watermark.\"\"\"\n","    batch_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n","    started = datetime.utcnow()\n","    lower, upper = get_window(signal)\n","    print(f\"[{signal}] window: {lower} -> {upper}\")\n","\n","    if upper is None or lower >= upper:\n","        print(f\"[{signal}] nothing to do\")\n","        return None\n","\n","    n_bronze = n_dlq = n_silver = n_dups = 0\n","    validated = None\n","\n","    lookups = load_lookups()\n","    \n","    try:\n","        validated, good, bad, n_bronze = validate(\n","        signal, lower, upper, lookups\n","        )\n","        n_dlq = write_dlq(bad, signal, batch_id, lower, upper)\n","        enriched = parse_and_enrich(good, signal)\n","        deduped, n_silver, n_dups = dedup_batch(enriched)\n","        merge_silver(deduped, signal)\n","    except Exception as e:\n","        # Failed run: log it, do NOT move the watermark, so the run can be repeated\n","        write_log(batch_id, signal, lower, upper, n_bronze, n_silver, n_dlq, n_dups,\n","                  \"FAILED\", started, str(e))\n","        raise\n","    finally:\n","        if validated is not None:\n","            validated.unpersist()\n","\n","    write_log(batch_id, signal, lower, upper, n_bronze, n_silver, n_dlq, n_dups,\n","              \"SUCCESS\", started)\n","    set_watermark(signal, upper)       # last step\n","\n","    balanced = (n_bronze == n_silver + n_dlq + n_dups)\n","    print(f\"[{signal}] bronze={n_bronze} silver={n_silver} dlq={n_dlq} dups={n_dups} | balanced={balanced}\")\n","    return dict(signal=signal, bronze=n_bronze, silver=n_silver, dlq=n_dlq, dups=n_dups)"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":15,"statement_ids":[15],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:35.0060472Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:21.9767907Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:22.1932869Z","parent_msg_id":"f154fa22-ee8d-4d00-be5c-fc6d77320e40"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 15, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"6e653d99-5fcf-4c0b-b46e-7880e2da281a"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Run batch job 1 for all signals, then Gate 1\n","`main()` calls `process_signal` for gps, engine, fuel and temperature, prints a balance table (bronze = silver + dlq + duplicates removed), then runs Gate 1.\n","\n","**Gate 1:** invalid share = DLQ rows / Bronze rows, overall and per signal. The status is FAIL when the overall share or any signal is above `GATE_MAX_INVALID_PCT` (5 percent). Silver is still written when the gate fails. The status JSON is written to `ops.ops_ingestion_log` (stage `GATE_1`, count columns NULL so sums over stage `BATCH` are not doubled) and returned by the exit cell, for example `{\"status\": \"PASS\", \"invalid_pct\": 1.0, ...}`.\n","\n","A second run with no new Bronze data prints \"nothing to do\" for each signal and returns PASS with the note \"no new data\"."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"2f096242-2828-4377-ae7a-72eb38b797c4"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def run_gate1(results, max_pct=GATE_MAX_INVALID_PCT):\n","    \"\"\"Gate 1: invalid share = DLQ rows / Bronze rows, overall and per signal. FAIL above max_pct.\"\"\"\n","    if not results:\n","        return {\"status\": \"PASS\", \"invalid_pct\": 0.0, \"threshold_pct\": max_pct,\n","                \"per_signal\": {}, \"failed_signals\": [], \"note\": \"no new data\"}\n","    per = {r[\"signal\"]: round(100.0 * r[\"dlq\"] / r[\"bronze\"], 3) if r[\"bronze\"] else 0.0 for r in results}\n","    tot_b = sum(r[\"bronze\"] for r in results)\n","    tot_d = sum(r[\"dlq\"] for r in results)\n","    overall = round(100.0 * tot_d / tot_b, 3) if tot_b else 0.0\n","    failed = [s for s, p in per.items() if p > max_pct]\n","    status = \"FAIL\" if (overall > max_pct or failed) else \"PASS\"\n","    return {\"status\": status, \"invalid_pct\": overall, \"threshold_pct\": max_pct,\n","            \"per_signal\": per, \"failed_signals\": failed,\n","            \"rows_bronze\": tot_b, \"rows_dlq\": tot_d}\n","\n","\n","def write_gate_log(gate, started):\n","    \"\"\"Same status JSON in ops.ops_ingestion_log (stage GATE_1). Count columns stay NULL so that\n","    sums over stage = 'BATCH' are not doubled.\"\"\"\n","    now = datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(tzinfo=None)\n","    row = [(str(uuid.uuid4()), None, JOB_NAME, \"ALL\", \"GATE_1\", None, None, None,\n","            None, None, None, None, gate[\"status\"], json.dumps(gate)[:1000], started, now)]\n","    ddl = (\"log_id string, batch_id string, job_name string, signal string, stage string, \"\n","           \"source_file string, window_start_utc string, window_end_utc string, \"\n","           \"rows_bronze long, rows_silver long, rows_dlq long, rows_duplicates_removed long, \"\n","           \"status string, error_message string, started_at timestamp, finished_at timestamp\")\n","    spark.createDataFrame(row, ddl).write.mode(\"append\").saveAsTable(\"ops.ops_ingestion_log\")\n","\n","\n","def main(signals=(\"gps\", \"engine\", \"fuel\", \"temperature\")):\n","    \"\"\"Batch job 1 for all signals, then Gate 1. Returns the gate status dict.\"\"\"\n","    started = datetime.now(timezone.utc).replace(tzinfo=None)\n","    results = []\n","    for s in signals:\n","        r = process_signal(s)\n","        if r:\n","            results.append(r)\n","\n","    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 60)\n","    print(f\"{'signal':12s} {'bronze':>8} {'silver':>8} {'dlq':>6} {'dups':>6} balanced\")\n","    for r in results:\n","        ok = r[\"bronze\"] == r[\"silver\"] + r[\"dlq\"] + r[\"dups\"]\n","        print(f\"{r['signal']:12s} {r['bronze']:>8} {r['silver']:>8} {r['dlq']:>6} {r['dups']:>6} {ok}\")\n","\n","    gate = run_gate1(results)\n","    write_gate_log(gate, started)\n","    print(\"GATE 1:\", json.dumps(gate))\n","    return gate"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":16,"statement_ids":[16],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:35.1524137Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:22.1955615Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:24.9017134Z","parent_msg_id":"31b885e9-d7c4-436c-84f1-efaab04ffe90"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 16, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"c6237a84-3c47-4e65-b16f-9230ef08ac80"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["gate = main()"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":17,"statement_ids":[17],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:35.3491616Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:24.9038991Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:38.294599Z","parent_msg_id":"e054c3b7-f23c-4849-b13e-e60a0f804a28"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 17, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipykernel_6713/2124151727.py:4: DeprecationWarning: datetime.datetime.utcnow() is deprecated and scheduled for removal in a future version. Use timezone-aware objects to represent datetimes in UTC: datetime.datetime.now(datetime.UTC).\n  started = datetime.utcnow()\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[gps] window: 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000 -> 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000\n[gps] nothing to do\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[engine] window: 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000 -> 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000\n[engine] nothing to do\n[fuel] window: 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000 -> 2026-10-26 04:55:08.178000\n[fuel] nothing to do\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[temperature] window: 2026-10-26 04:53:47.740000 -> 2026-10-26 04:53:47.740000\n[temperature] nothing to do\n\n============================================================\nsignal         bronze   silver    dlq   dups balanced\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["GATE 1: {\"status\": \"PASS\", \"invalid_pct\": 0.0, \"threshold_pct\": 5.0, \"per_signal\": {}, \"failed_signals\": [], \"note\": \"no new data\"}\n"]}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"f72b8a57-3575-4477-9f8d-9f21fb56a5c7"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Exit value\n","Returns the Gate 1 JSON as the notebook exit value so Airflow or a pipeline can read it. Run it last; it ends the notebook run."],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"ca3f7744-11bd-4bee-84c6-386b1cb98f22"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["mssparkutils.notebook.exit(json.dumps(gate))      # Airflow / pipeline reads this value"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":18,"statement_ids":[18],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-28T12:28:35.562405Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:38.2978206Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-28T12:29:38.9264279Z","parent_msg_id":"09b2431d-455d-4387-9ce8-224941ade4b3"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, b7362455-c515-428c-ab10-326de26e5b81, 18, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["ExitValue: {\"status\": \"PASS\", \"invalid_pct\": 0.0, \"threshold_pct\": 5.0, \"per_signal\": {}, \"failed_signals\": [], \"note\": \"no new data\"}"]}],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"674d98d0-341d-477b-9c1f-d75a9b1da595"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Release cached data and clear Spark cache\n","spark.catalog.clearCache()"],"outputs":[],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"1b7832fa-faf4-40e7-a1ca-43c2ca585d6c"}],"metadata":{"kernel_info":{"name":"synapse_pyspark"},"kernelspec":{"name":"synapse_pyspark","display_name":"synapse_pyspark"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark","ms_spell_check":{"ms_spell_check_language":"en"}},"nteract":{"version":"nteract-front-end@1.0.0"},"spark_compute":{"compute_id":"/trident/default","session_options":{"conf":{"spark.synapse.nbs.session.timeout":"1200000"}}},"dependencies":{"lakehouse":{"known_lakehouses":[{"id":"6b308346-999a-4674-9483-9c1c570f47cb"}],"default_lakehouse":"6b308346-999a-4674-9483-9c1c570f47cb","default_lakehouse_name":"lh_fleet","default_lakehouse_workspace_id":"bafd773a-fcc5-4c78-ae18-1eadf76f5da1"},"environment":{"environmentId":"dff35a10-3a68-4c1a-b16e-dd09d145a716","workspaceId":"bafd773a-fcc5-4c78-ae18-1eadf76f5da1"}}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}{"cells":[{"cell_type":"code","source":["from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n","from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n","from pyspark.sql.types import IntegerType, LongType, StringType\n","\n","spark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.session.timeZone\", \"UTC\")\n","\n","# Query URI: KQL database > Copy query URI (form https://<...>.kusto.data.microsoft.com)\n","KUSTO_URI = \"https://trd-s733h2caqmq2f44yrb.z3.kusto.fabric.microsoft.com\"\n","KUSTO_DB = \"eh_fleet\"\n","SIGNALS = [\"gps\", \"engine\", \"fuel\", \"temperature\", \"device_status\"]\n","SAFETY_LAG_MIN = 2\n","WM_TABLE = \"ops.ops_bronze_load_watermark\""],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":3,"statement_ids":[3],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:04.2534578Z","session_start_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:04.2545702Z","execution_start_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:11.9997885Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:12.2728317Z","parent_msg_id":"250e29b6-c3a3-4d3f-a6df-2bc08279f1de"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8, 3, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":1,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"4a047673-9b43-43ce-ac19-80329e40e981"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["spark.sql(\"CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS ops\")\n","spark.sql(f\"\"\"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS {WM_TABLE}\n","              (signal STRING, watermark_utc STRING, updated_at TIMESTAMP) USING DELTA\"\"\")\n","\n","FMT = \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\"\n","\n","def get_wm(signal):\n","    row = spark.sql(f\"SELECT watermark_utc FROM {WM_TABLE} WHERE signal='{signal}'\").first()\n","    s = row[0] if row else \"1900-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n","    return datetime.strptime(s, FMT).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n","\n","def set_wm(signal, wm):\n","    spark.sql(f\"DELETE FROM {WM_TABLE} WHERE signal='{signal}'\")\n","    spark.sql(f\"INSERT INTO {WM_TABLE} VALUES ('{signal}', '{wm.strftime(FMT)}', current_timestamp())\")\n","\n","def load_signal(signal, upper):\n","    kql_table = f\"bronze_{signal}_raw\"          # KQL table: no schema in KQL, name unchanged\n","    target = f\"bronze.bronze_{signal}_raw\"      # Lakehouse Delta table: schema.table\n","    lower = get_wm(signal)\n","    if lower >= upper:\n","        print(signal, \"nothing to do\"); return 0\n","\n","    query = f\"\"\"\n","    {kql_table}\n","    | where ingestion_time() >= datetime({lower.strftime(FMT)})\n","        and ingestion_time() <  datetime({upper.strftime(FMT)})\n","    | project raw_value, ingest_ts = ingestion_time()\n","    \"\"\"\n","    df = (spark.read.format(\"com.microsoft.kusto.spark.synapse.datasource\")\n","          .option(\"accessToken\", mssparkutils.credentials.getToken(KUSTO_URI))\n","          .option(\"kustoCluster\", KUSTO_URI)\n","          .option(\"kustoDatabase\", KUSTO_DB)\n","          .option(\"kustoQuery\", query)\n","          .load())\n","\n","    out = (df.withColumnRenamed(\"ingest_ts\", \"ingestion_time\")\n","             .withColumn(\"source_stream\", F.lit(signal))\n","             .withColumn(\"source_type\", F.lit(\"STREAM\"))\n","             .withColumn(\"ingestion_date\", F.to_date(\"ingestion_time\"))\n","             .withColumn(\"kafka_partition\", F.lit(None).cast(IntegerType()))\n","             .withColumn(\"kafka_offset\", F.lit(None).cast(LongType()))\n","             .withColumn(\"source_file\", F.lit(None).cast(StringType()))\n","             .withColumn(\"file_line\", F.lit(None).cast(IntegerType()))\n","             .select(\"raw_value\", \"source_stream\", \"source_type\", \"ingestion_time\",\n","                     \"ingestion_date\", \"kafka_partition\", \"kafka_offset\",\n","                     \"source_file\", \"file_line\")\n","             .cache())\n","    n = out.count()\n","\n","    # Retry guard: removes only rows of THIS window, in case an earlier attempt\n","    # wrote rows but failed before saving the watermark.\n","    if spark.catalog.tableExists(target):\n","        spark.sql(f\"\"\"DELETE FROM {target}\n","                      WHERE ingestion_time >= TIMESTAMP'{lower:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S}'\n","                        AND ingestion_time <  TIMESTAMP'{upper:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S}'\"\"\")\n","\n","    out.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"append\").partitionBy(\"ingestion_date\").saveAsTable(target)\n","    set_wm(signal, upper)\n","    out.unpersist()\n","    print(signal, \"loaded\", n)\n","    return n"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":4,"statement_ids":[4],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:16.7888342Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:16.7902074Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:20.2533027Z","parent_msg_id":"3fd9ff71-a506-4b97-8697-5f35cb24ad08"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8, 4, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":2,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"2747cd86-8a40-41de-ae04-181f5c3673bf"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["spark.table(WM_TABLE).show()      # check this before running, see the warning below\n","upper = (datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(minutes=SAFETY_LAG_MIN)).replace(microsecond=0)\n","for s in SIGNALS:\n","    load_signal(s, upper)\n","for s in SIGNALS:\n","    print(s, spark.table(f\"bronze.bronze_{s}_raw\").count())\n","mssparkutils.notebook.exit(\"done\")"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":5,"statement_ids":[5],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:27.7319817Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-26T04:58:27.7331212Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-26T05:01:37.1361875Z","parent_msg_id":"051a02a9-84cb-4084-ae6f-ce6fd05f9b62"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8, 5, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["gps loaded 30895\nengine loaded 30926\nfuel loaded 5176\ntemperature loaded 7197\ndevice_status loaded 0\ngps 30895\nengine 30926\nfuel 5176\ntemperature 7197\ndevice_status 0\n"]}],"execution_count":3,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"4b21bc00-b751-4d02-bdce-cce9cd3025bb"},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":6,"statement_ids":[6],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":false,"session_id":"ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-26T05:02:46.5331882Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-26T05:02:46.534474Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-26T05:02:49.4241808Z","parent_msg_id":"19c9a38c-c984-4720-9e07-508e9bad0513"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, ff22f24e-89a0-4a3a-a785-1fb2dec8c8c8, 6, Finished, Available, Finished, False)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"e4371598-5afc-4745-90b6-58e0bc8ed7ef"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Release cached data and clear Spark cache\n","spark.catalog.clearCache()"],"outputs":[],"execution_count":null,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"4b4f2bc4-c02c-4a4d-986f-132e55de0f70"}],"metadata":{"kernel_info":{"name":"synapse_pyspark"},"kernelspec":{"name":"synapse_pyspark","display_name":"synapse_pyspark"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark","ms_spell_check":{"ms_spell_check_language":"en"}},"nteract":{"version":"nteract-front-end@1.0.0"},"spark_compute":{"compute_id":"/trident/default","session_options":{"conf":{"spark.synapse.nbs.session.timeout":"1200000"}}},"dependencies":{"mirrored_db":{"known_mirrored_dbs":[{"id":"a2e0f787-aec6-47b4-b878-db7dcadb189b"}]},"lakehouse":{"known_lakehouses":[{"id":"6b308346-999a-4674-9483-9c1c570f47cb"}],"default_lakehouse":"6b308346-999a-4674-9483-9c1c570f47cb","default_lakehouse_name":"lh_fleet","default_lakehouse_workspace_id":"bafd773a-fcc5-4c78-ae18-1eadf76f5da1"}}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Cell 1 Views"],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"9156569c-ee13-4743-a8e6-074063a65f14"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["%%sql\n","CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW gold.v_in_gps AS\n","SELECT event_id, trip_id, vehicle_id, event_time, ingestion_time, dq_flags, latitude, longitude, speed_kmh, gps_accuracy_meters\n","FROM silver.silver_gps;\n","\n","CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW gold.v_in_engine AS\n","SELECT event_id, trip_id, vehicle_id, event_time, ingestion_time, dq_flags, engine_on, engine_rpm, engine_temperature_c, vehicle_speed_kmh\n","FROM silver.silver_engine;\n","\n","CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW gold.v_in_fuel AS\n","SELECT event_id, trip_id, vehicle_id, event_time, ingestion_time, dq_flags, fuel_level_liters, trip_fuel_used_liters, odometer_km\n","FROM silver.silver_fuel;\n","\n","CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW gold.v_in_temperature AS\n","SELECT event_id, trip_id, vehicle_id, event_time, ingestion_time, dq_flags, temperature_value AS temperature_c, sensor_status\n","FROM silver.silver_temperature;"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":8,"statement_ids":[5,6,7,8],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":true,"session_id":"a28a30e1-c1ac-4b6d-b217-1c2a6a75becb","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-27T23:37:35.5258465Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-27T23:37:35.5262881Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-27T23:37:42.0101594Z","parent_msg_id":"35813fd0-d06e-47dc-88d4-fdbcf6eedc40"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, a28a30e1-c1ac-4b6d-b217-1c2a6a75becb, 8, Finished, Available, Finished, True)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution_count":2,"data":{"application/vnd.synapse.sparksql-result+json":{"schema":{"type":"struct","fields":[]},"data":[],"truncated":false},"text/plain":"<Spark SQL result set with 0 rows and 0 fields>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution_count":2,"data":{"application/vnd.synapse.sparksql-result+json":{"schema":{"type":"struct","fields":[]},"data":[],"truncated":false},"text/plain":"<Spark SQL result set with 0 rows and 0 fields>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution_count":2,"data":{"application/vnd.synapse.sparksql-result+json":{"schema":{"type":"struct","fields":[]},"data":[],"truncated":false},"text/plain":"<Spark SQL result set with 0 rows and 0 fields>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution_count":2,"data":{"application/vnd.synapse.sparksql-result+json":{"schema":{"type":"struct","fields":[]},"data":[],"truncated":false},"text/plain":"<Spark SQL result set with 0 rows and 0 fields>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":1,"metadata":{"microsoft":{"language":"sparksql","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"},"collapsed":false},"id":"ccaee0d2-b42b-4535-addd-567813eb5a75"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Table DDL (this is the contract)"],"metadata":{"nteract":{"transient":{"deleting":false}},"microsoft":{"language":"python","language_group":"synapse_pyspark"}},"id":"166f5bb4-41a1-4935-a063-e0e723b7ce2b"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["%%sql\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.dim_vehicle (\n","  vehicle_key BIGINT, vehicle_id STRING, registration_number STRING,\n","  vehicle_type STRING, refrigeration_capable BOOLEAN, device_id STRING,\n","  fuel_type STRING, fuel_tank_capacity_liters DOUBLE, model_year INT,\n","  active_from TIMESTAMP, active_to TIMESTAMP,\n","  effective_from TIMESTAMP, effective_to TIMESTAMP, is_current BOOLEAN,\n","  type2_hash STRING, row_hash STRING\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.dim_driver (\n","  driver_key BIGINT, driver_id STRING, driver_name STRING, license_category STRING,\n","  hire_date DATE, active_from TIMESTAMP, active_to TIMESTAMP\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.dim_route (\n","  route_key BIGINT, route_id STRING, route_name STRING, origin_name STRING, destination_name STRING,\n","  planned_distance_km DOUBLE, allowed_deviation_meters INT, expected_duration_minutes INT,\n","  arrival_grace_minutes INT, speed_limit_kmh DOUBLE, checkpoint_count INT\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.dim_cargo_type (\n","  cargo_type_key BIGINT, cargo_type_id STRING, cargo_name STRING, is_temperature_controlled BOOLEAN,\n","  temperature_min_c DOUBLE, temperature_max_c DOUBLE, cargo_value_per_unit DOUBLE, currency_code STRING,\n","  max_excursion_minutes INT, spoilage_loss_pct DOUBLE, alert_hold_minutes INT\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.dim_date (\n","  date_key INT, date DATE, year INT, quarter INT, month INT, month_name STRING,\n","  day INT, day_of_week INT, day_name STRING, is_weekend BOOLEAN\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.fact_trip_performance (\n","  trip_id STRING,\n","  vehicle_key BIGINT, driver_key BIGINT, route_key BIGINT, cargo_type_key BIGINT, planned_start_date_key INT,\n","  vehicle_id STRING, driver_id STRING, route_id STRING, shipment_id STRING, cargo_type_id STRING,\n","  planned_start_time TIMESTAMP, planned_end_time TIMESTAMP, cargo_quantity DOUBLE, trip_status STRING,\n","  actual_start_time TIMESTAMP, actual_end_time TIMESTAMP, arrived BOOLEAN, arrival_status STRING, late_min DOUBLE,\n","  distance_km DOUBLE, fuel_used_l DOUBLE, fuel_l_per_100km DOUBLE, fuel_counter_anomalies BIGINT,\n","  engine_on_min DOUBLE, driving_min DOUBLE, idle_min_total DOUBLE, excessive_idle_min DOUBLE,\n","  speeding_min DOUBLE, deviation_episodes BIGINT,\n","  score_speeding_penalty DOUBLE, score_idling_penalty DOUBLE, score_deviation_penalty DOUBLE,\n","  score_lateness_penalty DOUBLE, trip_score DOUBLE, score_complete BOOLEAN,\n","  invalid_assignment BOOLEAN, has_telemetry BOOLEAN,\n","  gps_readings BIGINT, engine_readings BIGINT, fuel_readings BIGINT,\n","  first_event_time TIMESTAMP, last_event_time TIMESTAMP, built_at TIMESTAMP\n",") USING DELTA;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE  IF NOT EXISTS gold.fact_cold_chain (\n","  trip_id STRING, shipment_id STRING,\n","  vehicle_key BIGINT, driver_key BIGINT, route_key BIGINT, cargo_type_key BIGINT, planned_start_date_key INT,\n","  vehicle_id STRING, driver_id STRING, route_id STRING, cargo_type_id STRING,\n","  measured_min DOUBLE, in_range_min DOUBLE, out_range_min DOUBLE, unmeasured_min DOUBLE,\n","  min_temperature_c DOUBLE, max_temperature_c DOUBLE,\n","  excursion_episodes BIGINT, breach_episodes BIGINT, longest_excursion_min DOUBLE,\n","  breach_flag BOOLEAN, compromised_flag BOOLEAN, cargo_value DOUBLE, cargo_at_risk DOUBLE,\n","  suspect_readings BIGINT, temp_readings BIGINT, built_at TIMESTAMP\n",") USING DELTA;"],"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"application/vnd.livy.statement-meta+json":{"spark_pool":null,"statement_id":17,"statement_ids":[9,10,11,12,13,14,15,16,17],"state":"finished","livy_statement_state":"available","spark_jobs_updating":true,"session_id":"a28a30e1-c1ac-4b6d-b217-1c2a6a75becb","normalized_state":"finished","queued_time":"2026-10-27T23:39:41.5859867Z","session_start_time":null,"execution_start_time":"2026-10-27T23:39:41.5863626Z","execution_finish_time":"2026-10-27T23:39:53.3693764Z","parent_msg_id":"abbf2a27-0e82-4cea-a203-4fc1d88f40f6"},"text/plain":"StatementMeta(, a28a30e1-c1ac-4b6d-b217-1c2a6a75becb, 17, Finished, Available, Finished, True)"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution_count":3,"data":{"application/vnd.synapse.sparksql-result+json":{"schema":{"type":"struct","fields":[]},"data":[],"truncated":false},"text/plain":"<Spark SQL result set with 0 rows and 0 fields>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"execute_result","execution